From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 04:16:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] um: present the Darwin pointer as a direct touchscreen

The host frontend delivers absolute window coordinates plus mouse buttons,
and the guest exposed them as an INPUT_PROP_POINTER tablet with ABS_X/ABS_Y.
libinput accepts that shape, so the Linux desktop guests work, but Android
does not: EventHub classifies an absolute device only when it also reports
BTN_TOUCH, and a device that matches no class is dropped before InputReader
opens it. A booted Android 17 guest therefore listed only the keyboard in
"dumpsys input" and ignored every click.

Report BTN_TOUCH alongside BTN_LEFT and mark the device INPUT_PROP_DIRECT so
TouchInputMapper runs in direct mode and maps the absolute range onto the
display. REL_WHEEL is no longer consumed on Android; touch drag is the
native scrolling gesture there.

Change-Id: I29da7c53a5bd415d790b80a8ad5c2ec22dba3bae
---
 arch/um/drivers/vnc_input.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/um/drivers/vnc_input.c b/arch/um/drivers/vnc_input.c
index 5bc59c8a4381cb99d2297700b5e572a390b7387b..6ad13ee15181776f5cf62ecf149f1eadbbe1fc30 100644
--- a/arch/um/drivers/vnc_input.c
+++ b/arch/um/drivers/vnc_input.c
@@ -48,6 +48,8 @@ static void deliver_event(const struct uml_vnc_input_event *wire)
 	} else if (type == EV_ABS || type == EV_REL ||
 		   (type == EV_KEY && code >= BTN_MISC)) {
 		input_event(pointer, type, code, value);
+		if (type == EV_KEY && code == BTN_LEFT)
+			input_event(pointer, EV_KEY, BTN_TOUCH, value);
 	} else {
 		input_event(keyboard, type, code, value);
 	}
@@ -95,7 +97,18 @@ static void configure_pointer(struct input_dev *device)
 	device->name = "Darwin UML VNC Tablet";
 	device->phys = "uml/vnc/input1";
 	device->id.bustype = BUS_VIRTUAL;
-	__set_bit(INPUT_PROP_POINTER, device->propbit);
+	/*
+	 * Android's EventHub only recognises an absolute device when it reports
+	 * BTN_TOUCH together with ABS_X and ABS_Y. A bare INPUT_PROP_POINTER
+	 * tablet matches none of its classification rules, so it is dropped
+	 * before InputReader ever opens it and the guest sees no pointer at all.
+	 * INPUT_PROP_DIRECT then selects TouchInputMapper's direct mode, which
+	 * maps the absolute range straight onto the display - exactly what a
+	 * host window pointer already is. The mouse buttons stay so a click is
+	 * still reported as the primary button.
+	 */
+	__set_bit(INPUT_PROP_DIRECT, device->propbit);
+	input_set_capability(device, EV_KEY, BTN_TOUCH);
 	input_set_capability(device, EV_KEY, BTN_LEFT);
 	input_set_capability(device, EV_KEY, BTN_MIDDLE);
 	input_set_capability(device, EV_KEY, BTN_RIGHT);
